1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:15,760
With the global population predicted to hit close to 10 billion by 2050, and forecasts that agricultural production in some regions will need to nearly double to keep pace, food security is increasingly making headlines.
全球人口预计到2050年将接近100亿，而且有预测称，一些地区的农业产量需要增长近一倍才能跟上人口增长的步伐；在这种情况下，粮食安全越来越多地登上新闻头条。

2
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:23,660
In the UK, it has become a big talking point recently too, for a rather particular reason: Brexit.
在英国，这一问题最近也成了热门话题，原因相当特别：脱欧。

3
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,740
Brexit is seen by some as an opportunity to reverse a recent trend towards the UK importing food.
一些人把脱欧视为一个机会，可以借此扭转近来英国越来越多地进口食物的趋势。

4
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:38,540
The country produces only about 60 percent of the food it eats, down from almost three-quarters in the late 1980s.
英国自己生产的食物只占其消费量的60%左右，而在20世纪80年代末，这一比例还接近四分之三。

5
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:47,550
A move back to self-sufficiency, the argument goes, would boost the farming industry, political sovereignty and even the nation’s health.
按照这种观点，回归自给自足会提振农业，增强政治主权，甚至改善国民健康。

6
00:00:48,350 --> 00:00:51,470
Sounds great—but how feasible is this vision?
听起来很不错，但这一设想的可行性有多大呢？

7
00:00:52,270 --> 00:01:03,710
According to a report on UK food production from the University of Leeds, UK, 85 percent of the country’s total land area is associated with meat and dairy production.
根据英国利兹大学一份关于英国食物生产的报告，英国国土总面积的85%与肉类和奶制品生产相关。

8
00:01:04,510 --> 00:01:13,800
That supplies 80 percent of what is consumed, so even covering the whole country in livestock farms wouldn’t allow us to cover all our meat and dairy needs.
这部分生产供应了国内80%的消费量，因此，即使让畜牧场遍布全国，也无法满足我们对肉类和奶制品的全部需求。

9
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:18,350
There are many caveats to those figures, but they are still grave.
这些数字有许多需要附加说明之处，但依然很严峻。

10
00:01:19,150 --> 00:01:32,260
To become much more self-sufficient, the UK would need to drastically reduce its consumption of animal foods, and probably also farm more intensively—meaning fewer green fields and more factory-style production.
要大大提高自给程度，英国就需要大幅减少动物性食物的消费，而且可能还要更加集约地耕作——这意味着绿色田野会减少，工厂化生产会增加。

11
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:35,970
But switching to a mainly plant-based diet wouldn’t help.
但改为以植物性食物为主的饮食不会有什么帮助。

12
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:46,640
There is a good reason why the UK is dominated by animal husbandry: most of its terrain doesn’t have the right soil or climate to grow crops on a commercial basis.
英国以畜牧业为主是有充分理由的：该国大部分地区都没有适合商业化种植农作物的土壤或气候。

13
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:54,900
Just 25 percent of the country’s land is suitable for crop-growing, most of which is already occupied by arable fields.
英国只有25%的土地适合种植农作物，而其中大部分已经是耕地。

14
00:01:55,700 --> 00:02:09,860
Even if we converted all the suitable land to fields of fruit and veg—which would involve taking out all the nature reserves and removing thousands of people from their homes—we would achieve only a 30 percent boost in crop production.
即使我们把所有适合的土地都改造成果蔬田——这需要撤销所有自然保护区，让数以千计的人迁离家园——农作物产量也只能提高30%。

15
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:22,420
Just 23 percent of the fruit and vegetables consumed in the UK are currently home-grown, so even with the most extreme measures we could meet only 30 percent of our fresh produce needs.
目前，英国消费的水果和蔬菜中只有23%是本土种植的，因此，即使采取最极端的措施，我们也只能满足30%的新鲜农产品需求。

16
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:31,520
That is before we look for the space to grow the grains, sugars, seeds and oils that provide us with the vast bulk of our current calorie intake.
这还没考虑要为种植谷物、糖料、种子和油料作物寻找空间，而目前我们摄入的热量绝大部分都来自这些作物。
